[
  {
    "comment": "Structural ceramics in BLOCK form. The drop-breakage predicate is the block material, and `blockmaterial: \"Ceramic\"` turns out to be far wider than pottery: 60 vanilla blocktypes carry it, including every brick and tile course, the bloomery, the clay oven, the kiln door, and six aquatic overlay blocks that have nothing to do with clay at all. Their ITEM forms (burnedbrick, claytile, shingle) are exempt for free because an item has no block material. Greenware needs no entry here either: it is excluded generically by still having fire-type combustible properties. Third-party mods can opt out the same way, by setting this attribute, with no change to Rudiments.",
    "file": "game:blocktypes/clay/bloomerybase",
    "op": "addmerge",
    "path": "/attributes",
    "value": {
      "rudiments": {
        "unbreakableOnDrop": true
      }
